## Why This Is Asked

This question probes real-world streaming semantics, multi-tenant isolation, and data contracts in GCP with practical rollback.

## Key Concepts

- Dataflow exactly-once processing
- Tenant-level dedupe by (tenant_id, txn_id)
- Watermarks for late events
- Parquet in Cloud Storage + incremental BigQuery loading
- Data Catalog contracts and lineage
- 24h rollback and backfill test plan

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo Dataflow-like dedupe (illustrative)
class DedupFn {
  process(element) {
    const key = element.tenant_id + '|' + element.txn_id;
    if (!state.has(key)) {
      state.add(key);
      return element;
    }
    return null;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify exactly-once behavior under backpressure and late data?
- How would you roll back a fraudulent day’s data within 24h?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesss ability to design scalable, privacy-preserving streaming pipelines with per-tenant controls and lineage. It also tests cross-region delivery and data-exchange mechanics.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped masking and schema versioning
- Streaming ingestion: Pub/Sub + Dataflow
- Per-tenant partitioned analytics in BigQuery
- End-to-end lineage via Data Catalog; sharing via Data Exchange
- 24h per-tenant rollback using raw logs in Cloud Storage

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Dataflow masking (simplified)
function maskPII(event) {
  event.email = hash(event.email).slice(0,8) + "@masked";
  // mask other PII fields
  return event;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test rollout and rollback for 24h per-tenant in production?
- How would you detect and handle schema drift across tenants/regions?
